WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.040
NARRATOR: Maria has spotted
the fresh tracks of a snake

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.171
in the sand, and
it could still be

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.674
hiding somewhere in the tomb.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.060
John joins them to
lend some support.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.780
Good luck.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:23.423
OK, if you're still in
here, I come in peace.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.262
Tapping a bit.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:31.831
Maria, don't tap
it, just lift it.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.133
Yank it.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.302
I don't want it to end
up falling on our mummy.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.480
JOHN: Just be safe.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.740
NARRATOR: Many of the
snakes in Egypt are deadly.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.860
JOHN: You OK?

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.880
Yeah, there's tracks.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.215
Lift the stone.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.750
You want to keep back
from the door, please.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.792
I got it.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:00:59.859
Well.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:00.980
JOHN: Nothing?

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:04.900
I tell you what.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:05.899
I'm going to carry
on with my work

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.535
and leave you with your snake.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.737
NARRATOR: Maria and
Tricia can't be completely

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.039
sure the snake is gone.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:16.075
I removed a hole
where it ended.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.277
OK.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.913
You scared him off
anyway, I think.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.448
NARRATOR: But with
the clock ticking,

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.716
they decide they must press on.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.719
We have to be careful to
distinguish what is mummy

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:27.987
and what is dirt here.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:28.822
Yes.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.757
This stone can go.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:33.059
NARRATOR: By excavating
the body from the mud,

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:36.396
they hope to discover more
about the role of this person

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:40.767
in Gebel El Silsileh community,
but the state of the mummy

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.669
makes their task tougher.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:43.336
More pieces.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.038
Little piece of skull.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.773
Yeah, I got more here.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.241
Burnt.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:54.581
They burn to such heat that
the white bones turn blue.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.050
NARRATOR: Ancient looters
would often burn the mummies

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.652
they found inside a tomb.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.622
They're after gold and
by burning the mummies,

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.391
it's easier for them
to open them up.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.861
Very sad.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.796
NARRATOR: The ancient
Egyptians would have dreaded

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.631
this kind of mutilation.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:14.367
They went to huge lengths
to mummify and protect

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:18.004
their dead believing that
to succeed in the afterlife,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.960
key elements of the body and
soul must be preserved intact.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.300
The first was the Ren,
your identity and name.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:32.151
It lived for as long as
your name was spoken.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:35.121
Ib was the heart, the
seat of your soul,

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:37.657
the good force in your life.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.927
Sheut was the shadow,
an image of yourself that was

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.397
reborn every day at sunrise.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.833
Ba was the unique personality.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.671
It left the body in the form of
a bird at night and at death.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:54.941
The Ka was the vital
essence, the force

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:58.011
that animated the individual.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.881
And the Khat was the physical
form of the body, which must

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.851
be preserved or mummified
for the dead to be granted

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:05.960
eternal life.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.980
I feel like I personally
get attached when I'm working

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:15.995
on a mummy, and you feel like
you're getting to know them,

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.780
and you feel like a caretaker.

